  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights Institute of South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Human Rights Institute of South Africa (HURISA) is a specialised human rights NGO; supporting advocacy, activism, mobilisation, public education and awareness-raising in human rights in South Africa for 25 years, since the fall of apartheid. The Danish Embassy cooperation with HURISA will enable the organisation, on a broad scale, to engage in human rights awareness-raising at local, provincial and national levels. The grant helped to develop several human rights dialogues in the country that will produce consolidated reports on the progress and solutions for effectively implementing human rights in South Africa. It assisted to develop human rights education and communication materials and tools to distribute to targeted groups in South Africa &#x2013; including the South African National Assembly Parliament. The project aims to sustain a nation-wide discourse on the importance of human rights.</narrative>
  </description>
